            0.849,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(k) Handy Hundreds says, “There are some numbers which Tedious Tens and Thoughtful Thousands can’t show but I can.” Is this statement true? Think and explore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.365,
            0.6,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Creative Chitti",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a different kind of calculator. It has the following buttons: +1, +10, +100, +1000, +10000, +100000 and +1000000. It always has multiple ways of doing things. “How so?”, you might ask. To get the number 321, it presses +10 thirty two times and +1 once. Will it get 321? Alternatively, it can press +100 two times and +10 twelve times and +1 once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.608,
            0.369,
            0.892,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.608,
                0.369,
                0.892,
                0.529
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.537,
            0.593,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Two of the many different ways to get 5072 are shown below: These two ways can be expressed as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.597,
            0.577,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) (50 × 100) + (7 × 10) + (2 × 1) = 5072"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.621,
            0.582,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) (3×1000) + (20×100) + (72 ×1) = 5072"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.649,
            0.588,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find a different way to get 5072 and write an expression for the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.709,
            0.293,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.735,
            0.59,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For each number given below, write expressions for at least two different ways to obtain the number through button clicks. Think like Chitti and be creative."
            }
          ]
        },
